{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Prime.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_deuteron_frobenius_not_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_deuteron_frobenius_not_unit","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L160-L167","doc":"**QOU deuteron instance**, C = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1) = 192.\n(Was stated at -32 until 2026-08-23. Bean `qou-lrnd`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_proton_frobenius_not_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_proton_frobenius_not_unit","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L149-L158","doc":"**QOU proton/neutron instance**, C = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1) = 8.\n(Was stated at 4 until 2026-08-23; `a₀` is the constant 8. Bean\n`qou-lrnd`.) Note this instance does NOT separate proton from neutron —\nafter the `tr_M` denominator both collapse to `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.habiro_frobenius_not_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.habiro_frobenius_not_unit","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L106-L147","doc":"**The perpetual obstruction, with the prime in the statement.**\n\n`frob p` is the Frobenius at `p` — `f(u)|_{u = ζ_{2p}}` from the Habiro\nexpansion, living in `ℤ[ζ_{2p}]` — and `reduce p` is reduction modulo the\nprime ideal `𝔭 = (1 - ζ_p)`. The collapse identity `reduce p (frob p) = C`\nis the content the symbolic derivation supplies: at `q = ζ_{2p}` one has\n`q ≡ -1 (mod 𝔭)` and `(q;q)_m ≡ 0 (mod 𝔭)` for `m ≥ 2`, so the expansion\ncollapses to `a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1) = C`.\n\nUnlike `qou_proton_perpetual_obstruction`, the conclusion here is about\n`frob p` rather than about a constant, so `p` is not decoration.\n\n🛑 **The hypotheses have no instantiation at the ring the paragraph above\ndescribes** (2026-08-23, bean `qou-lrnd`). The theorem is true and\nsorry-free for an arbitrary family `R` carrying a hom to `ℤ` — that is not\nin question — but it does not reach the QOU Frobenius, for two independent\nreasons, both checked exactly in\n`computations/probes/cyclotomic_residue_four_unit_probe.py`:\n\n* `reduce p : R p →+* ℤ` cannot be reduction mod `𝔭`. That map lands in\n  `O/𝔭 ≅ 𝔽_p`. And no hom `ℤ[ζ_2p] →+* ℤ` sends `ζ ↦ -1` — it would force\n  `Φ_2p(-1) = 0`, whereas `Φ_2p(-1) = p`. (None exists at all.)\n* With the correct target `𝔽_p`, the residue `C` is a **unit** for every\n  `p ∤ C`, so `not_isUnit_of_image` — which needs the *residue* to be a\n  non-unit — runs the wrong way. This is not a gap awaiting a proof: the\n  cyclotomic unit `u₄ = 1 + ζ + ζ² + ζ³` is a unit of `ℤ[ζ_p]` with\n  residue exactly `4 (mod 𝔭)`, so `Frob_p ≡ 4 (mod 𝔭)` is *compatible\n  with `Frob_p` being a unit*.\n\nThe collapse half is fine and is now proved in general, with no cyclotomic\ninput: `QOU.LiftingDescent.map_habiro_expansion`. What is missing is a\ndifferent obstruction argument entirely, not a discharge of `h_collapse`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.not_isUnit_of_image","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.not_isUnit_of_image","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L100-L104","doc":"Non-unitness transfers backwards along a ring map: a ring hom carries\nunits to units, so a non-unit image forces a non-unit source. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.perpetual_obstruction_from_collapse_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.perpetual_obstruction_from_collapse_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L90-L98","doc":"The prime-ideal-collapse invariant C is a rational integer derived\nfrom the Habiro expansion: C = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1). When |C| > 1,\nthe perpetual obstruction follows with an EMPTY exception set\n(i.e., the Frobenius is non-unit at EVERY prime, not just\n\"almost every\"). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_deuteron_perpetual_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_deuteron_perpetual_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L77-L88","doc":"**The collapse invariant for the deuteron is not a unit.**\nC = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1) = 192, and |192| > 1.\n\n🛑 This said `-32` until 2026-08-23. The deuteron's `a₀` is the constant\n**192** and `a₁(-1) = 0`, so C = 192 (bean `qou-lrnd`; probe as above).\n\nSame reading as the proton above: the conclusion is `¬IsUnit (192 : ℤ)`,\na fact about one integer. `qou_deuteron_frobenius_not_unit` is the\nstatement about the Frobenius. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_proton_perpetual_obstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.qou_proton_perpetual_obstruction","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L29-L75","doc":"**The collapse invariant for the proton/neutron is not a unit.**\n\nC = a₀(-1) + 2·a₁(-1) = 8 for the proton, and |8| > 1.\n\n(This said \"= 4 for the proton and neutron\" until 2026-08-23. Both halves\nwere wrong: `a₀` is 8 for the proton and **2** for the neutron, so they do\nnot share a numerator constant. Bean `qou-lrnd`.)\n\nNOTE (2026-08-22, bean `qou-lrnd`): read the TYPE. The conclusion is\n`¬IsUnit (4 : ℤ)`, which mentions neither `p` nor `S`, and the proof term\ndiscards both binders and takes `S = ∅`. So what this proves is that 4 is\nnot a unit in ℤ — not that the Frobenius is a non-unit at every prime.\nThe statement carrying that is `qou_proton_frobenius_not_unit` below,\nwhose conclusion is `¬ IsUnit (frob p)`. Kept because it is cited, and\nbecause the ∃/∀ shape is what makes it compose with\n`perpetual_obstruction_from_trace`.\n\nDerivation: at q = ζ_{2p}, the prime ideal 𝔭 = (1-ζ_p) satisfies\nq ≡ -1 (mod 𝔭), and (q;q)_m ≡ 0 (mod 𝔭) for m ≥ 2. Therefore\nFrob_p ≡ a₀(-1) + a₁(-1)·(1-(-1)) = 8 + 0 = 8 (mod 𝔭).\nCORRECTION (2026-08-23, bean `qou-lrnd`): this paragraph previously\ncontinued \"The Galois norm N(Frob_p) ≡ 4^{p-1} (mod p), which is never ±1\nfor p ≥ 3\". That is wrong twice: by Fermat 4^{p-1} ≡ 1 (mod p) whenever\np ∤ 4, and 1 ≡ +1, so the congruence is *satisfied* by a unit rather than\nexcluded by one. The claim is removed rather than repaired -- see\n`HabiroCollapse.lean`, where the inference it was standing in for is shown\nnot to hold at all.\n\nThis proof uses only the STRUCTURE of the Habiro expansion, not\n🛑 **C IS 8, NOT 4** (2026-08-23, bean `qou-lrnd`). This read \"The value\nC=4 is an exact algebraic identity: a₀(u) evaluated at u=-1 gives 4, and\na₁(-1)=0.\" Half of that holds — `a₁(-1) = 0` — but `a₀` is the **constant\n8** for the proton (and 2 for the neutron, 192 for the deuteron), so no\nevaluation point yields 4. Measured from the canonical coefficients witness\nin `computations/probes/habiro_collapse_constant_probe.py`. The statement\nbelow is re-stated at 8; `1 < natAbs` is unaffected.\n\nAnd `tr_M` carries a denominator: dividing through, proton and neutron\nboth collapse to `1/2` and the deuteron to `1/8` — not integers, and the\ncollapse does not separate proton from neutron.\n\nRef: [thm:motivic-perpetual-obstruction]\nRef: [def:motivic-galois-character]\nRef: bean qou-86gm (symbolic derivation) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.perpetual_obstruction_from_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.perpetual_obstruction_from_trace","kind":"theorem","line":14,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L14-L27","doc":"Given a trace function and a bound N past which the trace is large, \nthe trace is not a unit almost everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.LiftingDescent.galois_trace_not_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.LiftingDescent.galois_trace_not_unit","kind":"theorem","line":7,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/LiftingDescent/MotivicPerpetualObstructionFromTrace.lean#L7-L12","doc":"In ℤ, the only units are ±1. If |trace| > 1 then it's not a unit.\nThis is the Route A proof: bypass the abstract Mhat and work in ℤ. ","signatureChunk":0}]}